    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear objective: capitalize on high-upside matchups to close the gap in our 5x5 standing. **Corbin Carroll** (84.65) and **James Wood** (78.41) anchor our outfield, standing as our two highest-rated options. **Corbin Carroll** benefits immensely from his leadoff role and a favorable matchup against M. Keller, while **James Wood** is perfectly positioned to exploit a weak 5.89 xERA from Scherzer, carrying an elite 0.420 xwOBA that makes him a must-start despite the high-profile opposition. **Jose Caballero** also grades out as a premier play at 71.83; his +13% platoon edge against Schultz makes him an essential component of our pursuit of stolen bases, which remains our primary focus as we hunt for efficiency in the speed category.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational variables as we finalize the card. **Austin Riley** (54.87) carries the most risk today, as a 31% rain probability threatens his presence in the lineup, and his efficiency is hampered by a tough draw against a left-handed arm. The most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Henry Bolte** (51.08) on the outside looking in. While **Henry Bolte** carries strong potential and benefits from a +10% park factor, his lower base projection relative to our starting outfielders kept him tethered to the bench; he remains our top insurance policy should the rain in **Austin Riley**'s game force a late-inning pivot. We are also keeping a close eye on **Isaac Paredes** and **Brice Turang**, whose scores remain subject to minor fluctuations pending final lineup releases, though both are locked into strong slots should their projected spots at #3 and #2 hold firm.",
